## Director mode

For any multi-task or multi-file feature build, load the `agent-director`
skill and operate as director: plan, decompose into task contracts,
delegate each task to a subagent (implementer), and independently review
before accepting. Every state-changing or code task, including a small or
unambiguous fix, uses a complete task contract and an implementer. A
zero-worker contract is allowed only for a purely read-only task marked
`read_only: true`; any takeover remains governed by the skill's recorded
takeover template.

- Skill location: `.claude/skills/agent-director/` (project) or
  `~/.claude/skills/agent-director/` (user-global).
- The default profile (`profiles/default.yaml` next to the skill) applies
  automatically — no selection needed. It does not pick which model is
  director (that's always whichever model is running this session); it sets
  non-cap policy such as `failure_threshold` and `effort_by_task_kind`. Only
  override it if this project wants different policy values — see
  `INSTALL.md` → "The default profile."
- Native runtime capacity is the only worker-capacity authority. If capacity
  telemetry is unavailable, keep it `unknown`; do not invent a numeric project
  cap. A slot-full response requires waiting, inspecting evidence, closing
  completed workers, then re-scoping or returning to the user.
